course: dictionary
lesson: 9017
title: Words from games
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words are names for things you can play with. «There is a skittle-alley» in the sentence tells you that a skittle-alley is a place to play. The words around skittle help you work out what it is: alley is a lane or path, so a skittle-alley is a lane for a game.
explain: A skittle is a wooden or plastic piece shaped like a bottle. Players try to knock them down with a ball. The game is also called skittles, and it is an older cousin of ten-pin bowling.
explain: Words can also make phrases that mean something different from their parts. «Knocked down like skittles» does not mean that you are a skittle. It means many things falling over quickly, one after another.
fact: A skittle is a bottle-shaped piece used in a game.
fact: Skittles is the name of the game where players knock the pieces down with a ball.
fact: Skittles is an older cousin of ten-pin bowling.
fact: «Knocked down like skittles» means many things falling quickly.
fact: «Life is not all beer and skittles» (UK, old) means life is not all fun.
exercise: In the sentence «There is a skittle-alley», what is skittles? | A type of goldfish | A kind of flower in the pond | *The name of a game like bowling | A small wooden boat
exercise: Children set up skittles and roll a ball at them. What do the players try to do? | Catch the skittles in a net | Paint the skittles gold | Hide the skittles under a table | *Knock the skittles down with the ball
exercise: What does the phrase «knocked down like skittles» mean? | *Many things falling over quickly | Something very heavy and hard to move | A slow, careful walk | People dancing in a circle
test: Which word means a game like bowling? | Pond | Border | Pile | *Skittles
test: «Life is not all beer and skittles» means: | Life is full of games to play | Life is always sweet, like a drink | *Life is not all fun | Life is only about sport
exam: In «There is a skittle-alley», what tells you that a skittle-alley is a place for a game? | The word glass, which is in the sentence | The word pond, which is near it | *The word alley, a lane, next to skittle | The word border, which is a kind of pattern
